{"content":[{"c":["LASEA"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Seaport city on the island of Crete, about five miles (8 kilometers) east of Fair Havens. Paul’s ship passed Lasea on its way to Italy (",{"href":"?bref=Acts.27.8","r":"Acts.27.8","rawR":"Acts.27.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.27.8","value":"Acts.27.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 27:8"},"). Little is known about Lasea; it is probably in ruins near Fair Havens. It may be the same as the Lasos that Pliny the Elder mentions in his ",{"c":["Natural History"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," (4.12.59). He says it was famous in the ancient world, for its region contained 100 cities and it was one of Crete’s most important ports."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Lasea","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Acts 27:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Acts.27.8","rawQueryValue":"Acts.27.8","sourceRefExact":"Acts.27.8"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"86c064e45df13e028be6494423117f2859f6f86bc9de945c5a958774f3bb6afe","sourceItemName":"Lasea","sourceItemOrder":32,"sourceMember":"Articles/L.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Lasea","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Lasea","title":"Lasea","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}